628:
(a) It shall be unlawful to drive any vehicle in excess of 12,500 pounds gross vehicle weight (GVW) on any street within the city limits, unless said vehicle is making a local pickup or delivery, except on the following state highways and county roads, to wit: Georgia Highways 14, 54 and 100; county roads Mountville-Hogansville Road, Bass Cross Road and Mobley Bridge Road.
(b) It shall be unlawful to park any vehicle in excess of 12,500 pounds gross vehicle weight (GVW) on any street in the city limits, public parking areas, public right-of-way, public land, or private property (unless said private property is zoned commercial or industrial) unless such vehicle has a valid truck parking permit issued by the city manager.
(c) In issuing a permit to park a vehicle in excess of 12,500 pounds gross vehicle weight (GVW), the city manager shall receive and consider the following:
(1) Application for truck-parking permit in the format established by the city manager;
(2) A scaled sketch of the proposed parking site;
(3) A photograph of the area proposed for vehicle parking;
(4) Appropriateness of proposed parking place for vehicle;
(5) Appropriateness of route of vehicle to and from proposed parking place and ability of such roadway to support such vehicle traffic;
(6) Public comments made during a ten-day public comment period; and
(7) Whether, in the opinion of the city manager, the proposed permit would adversely affect the neighborhood at issue.
(d) No tractor-trailer combination will be eligible for the parking permit established herein.
(e) Permits shall be issued on a calendar year basis at a cost as may be established from time to time by the city council. Permits will be prorated for any partial year on a quarterly basis.
(f) All persons found guilty of a violation of this ordinance shall be punished in accordance with section 1-7 of the Code.
(Code 1988, § 5-1-8; Ord. No. 07-04-02-B, § 1, 4-2-2007; Ord. No. 13-04-15A, § 1, 4-15-2013; Ord. No. 15-06-01, § 1, 6-1-2015)

